    Probe: walk infers a generic dotted method's own static arguments (row 21)

    Edits the original tree, on the probe branch only. A dotted call that
    writes no static argument to a generic method, which an object holds as
    its symbolic instance, now infers the instance from the arguments' types
    through EvaluatorBase.inferAndInstantiateGenericFunction, in the generic
    method's evaluation environment (DottedMethodApplication). An overloaded
    method set treats such a symbolic instance as its generic method when it
    chooses and instantiates an overload (OverloadedFunction.bestMatchInternal
    and bestMatchWithCoercion). The expected-failure test XXXMethodStaticArgRungT
    is promoted to MethodStaticArgInference.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
